# Composing functions

## `Function` — mind the order

```java
times2.andThen(plus1).apply(10);   // 21 — times2 FIRST, then plus1
times2.compose(plus1).apply(10);   // 22 — plus1 first, then times2
```

- **`f.andThen(g)`** — `f`, then `g` (execution order — prefer this)
- **`f.compose(g)`** — `g` first, then `f` (`f(g(x))`)

## `Predicate` — boolean logic

```java
Predicate<String> valid = nonBlank.and(shortish);
list.removeIf(nonBlank.negate());   // and · or · negate
```

Each returns a **new** predicate; originals untouched.

## `Consumer.andThen` · `Comparator`

```java
orders.forEach(log.andThen(save));                 // both, same input
comparing(Person::lastName).thenComparing(Person::firstName);
```

## Why

Readability · reuse · testability → the model behind **streams**:
`filter(p).map(f).forEach(c)`
